 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "eruvin.99a.16",
   "daf": "99a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "אָמַר רֵישׁ לָקִישׁ: כִּיַּח בִּפְנֵי רַבּוֹ חַיָּיב מִיתָה, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר ״כׇּל מְשַׂנְאַי אָהֲבוּ מָוֶת״ — אַל תִּקְרֵי ״לִמְשַׂנְאַי״, אֶלָּא ״לְמַשְׂנִיאַי״.",
   "en": "Having mentioned phlegm, the Gemara cites a related teaching: «Reish Lakish said:» One who expelled «phlegm in front of his master» has acted in a disrespectful manner and is «liable for» the punishment of «death» at the hand of Heaven, «as it is stated: “All they who hate Me love death”» (Proverbs 8:36). «Do not read it» as: «“They who hate [mesanai] Me”; rather,» read it as: «“Those who make themselves hateful [masniai] to Me,”» i.e., those who make themselves hateful by such a discharge."
  },
  {
   "id": "eruvin.99a.17",
   "daf": "99a",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "וְהָא מֵינָס אֲנִיס? כִּיַּח וְרָק קָאָמְרִינַן.",
   "en": "The Gemara expresses surprise at this ruling: «But doesn’t he» do so «involuntarily,» as no one coughs and emits phlegm by choice; why should this be considered a transgression? The Gemara answers: «We are speaking» here of someone who had «phlegm» in his mouth «and spat» it out, i.e., one who had the opportunity to leave his master’s presence and spit outside."
  }
 ],
